uses":50},{"base":"H3379","lemma":"יָֽרָבְעָם","tr":"ya·rov·am","gloss":"Jeroboam","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":104},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":877},{"base":"H6235","lemma":"עֶשֶׂר","tr":"e·ser","gloss":"ten","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":176},{"base":"H2398","lemma":"חָטָא","tr":"cha·ta","gloss":"to sin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":238}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":14,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"For the LORD saw that the affliction of the Israelites, both slave and free, was very bitter. There was no one to help Israel,","from":4},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The LORD said, “I have indeed seen the affliction of My people in Egypt. I have heard them crying out because of their oppressors, and I am aware of their sufferings.","from":4},{"book":"1KI","chapter":16,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then he set up an Asherah pole. Thus Ahab did more to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger than all the kings of Israel before him.","from":6},{"book":"1KI","chapter":19,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Jehu will put to death whoever escapes the sword of Hazael, and Elisha will put to death whoever escapes the sword of Jehu.","from":3},{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"When Hazael king of Aram died, his son Ben-hadad reigned in his place.","from":3},{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Jehoash son of Jehoahaz took back from Ben-hadad son of Hazael the cities that Hazael had taken in battle from his father Jehoahaz. Jehoash defeated Ben-hadad three times, and so recovered the cities of Israel.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":78,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When He slew them, they would seek Him; they repented and searched for God.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then God heard the voice of the boy, and the angel of God called to Hagar from heaven, “What is wrong, Hagar? Do not be afraid, for God has heard the voice of the boy where he lies.","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"10-13":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"joash-h3101j","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jehoahaz-h3059g","name":"Jehoahaz","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"joash-h3101i","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"nebat-h5028","name":"Nebat","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jeroboam","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"amaziah-h0558g","name":"Amaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379h","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":10}],"words":[{"base":"H3101","lemma":"יוֹאָשׁ","tr":"yo·ash","gloss":"Joash","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":47},{"base":"H3379","lemma":"יָֽרָבְעָם","tr":"ya·rov·am","gloss":"Jeroboam","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":104},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":877},{"base":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","tr":"sho·me·ron","gloss":"Samaria","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820},{"base":"H3060","lemma":"יְהוֹאָשׁ","tr":"ye·ho·ash","gloss":"Jehoash","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H3059","lemma":"יְהוֹאָחָז","tr":"ye·ho·a·chaz","gloss":"Jehoahaz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H5028","lemma":"נְבָט","tr":"ne·vat","gloss":"Nebat","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25},{"base":"H0558","lemma":"אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·mats·yah","gloss":"Amaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":40}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when your days are fulfilled and you rest with your fathers, I will raise up your descendant after you, who will come from your own body, and I will establish his kingdom.","from":13},{"book":"1KI","chapter":1,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Otherwise, when my lord the king rests with his fathers, I and my son Solomon will be counted as criminals.”","from":13},{"book":"1KI","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then David rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David.","from":13},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and said to Jeroboam, “Take ten pieces for yourself, for this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Behold, I will tear the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon, and I will give you ten tribes.","from":13},{"book":"2KI","chapter":3,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Nevertheless, he clung to the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit; he did not turn away from them.","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":10,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"but he did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit—the worship of the golden calves at Bethel and Dan.","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and followed the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit; he did not turn away from them.","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Nevertheless, they did not turn away from the sins that the house of Jeroboam had caused Israel to commit, but they continued to walk in them. The Asherah pole even remained standing in Samaria.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"14-19":{"people":[{"id":"elisha-h0477","name":"Elisha","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":4,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"joash-h3101j","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"aphek-h0663i","name":"Aphek","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"words":[{"base":"H2671","lemma":"חֵץ","tr":"chets","gloss":"arrow","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":53},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":500},{"base":"H0477","lemma":"אֱלִישָׁע","tr":"e·li·sah","gloss":"Elisha","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":58},{"base":"H0758","lemma":"אֲרָם","tr":"a·ram","gloss":"Aram","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":143},{"base":"H7198","lemma":"קֶ֫שֶׁת","tr":"qe·shet","gloss":"bow","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":76},{"base":"H6471","lemma":"פַּ֫עַם","tr":"pa·am","gloss":"beat","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":118},{"base":"H3947","lemma":"לָקַח","tr":"la·qach","gloss":"to take: take","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":966},{"base":"H8668","lemma":"תְּשׁוּעָה","tr":"te·shu·ah","gloss":"deliverance: salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":34},{"base":"H7392","lemma":"רָכַב","tr":"ra·khav","gloss":"to ride","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":78},{"base":"H3384","lemma":"יָרָא","tr":"ya·ra","gloss":"to shoot","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":80}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then Jehoash son of Jehoahaz took back from Ben-hadad son of Hazael the cities that Hazael had taken in battle from his father Jehoahaz. Jehoash defeated Ben-hadad three times, and so recovered the cities of Israel.","from":19},{"book":"1KI","chapter":20,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"In the spring, Ben-hadad mobilized the Arameans and went up to Aphek to fight against Israel.","from":17},{"book":"2KI","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As Elisha watched, he cried out, “My father, my father, the chariots and horsemen of Israel!” And he saw Elijah no more. So taking hold of his own clothes, he tore them in two.","from":14},{"book":"PHP","chapter":2,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For he has been longing for all of you and is distressed because you heard he was ill.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Some time later Joseph was told, “Your father is ill.” So he set out with his two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Yet he steadied his bow, and his strong arms were tempered by the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob, in the name of the Shepherd, the Rock of Israel,","from":16},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the LORD asked him, “What is that in your hand?” “A staff,” he replied.","from":17},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But take this staff in your hand so you can perform signs with it.”","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"20-25":{"people":[{"id":"elisha-h0477","name":"Elisha","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"hazael-h2371","name":"Hazael","kind":"person","brief":"Syrian king","count":3,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"jehoahaz-h3059g","name":"Jehoahaz","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"ben-hadad-h1130i","name":"Ben-hadad","kind":"person","brief":"Syrian king","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"joash-h3101j","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":22}],"words":[{"base":"H1130","lemma":"בֶּן־הֲדַד","tr":"ben-ha·dad","gloss":"Ben-hadad","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":50},{"base":"H3059","lemma":"יְהוֹאָחָז","tr":"ye·ho·a·chaz","gloss":"Jehoahaz","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":20},{"base":"H2371","lemma":"חֲזָהאֵל","tr":"cha·za·el","gloss":"Hazael","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":23},{"base":"H0477","lemma":"אֱלִישָׁע","tr":"e·li·sah","gloss":"Elisha","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":58},{"base":"H1416","lemma":"גְּדוּד","tr":"ge·dud","gloss":"band","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"H7993","lemma":"שָׁלַךְ","tr":"sha·lakh","gloss":"to throw","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":125},{"base":"H6912","lemma":"קָבַר","tr":"qa·var","gloss":"to bury","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":133},{"base":"H0758","lemma":"אֲרָם","tr":"a·ram","gloss":"Aram","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":143},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":840},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":929}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"He remembers His covenant forever, the word He ordained for a thousand generations—","from":23},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So God heard their groaning, and He remembered His covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.","from":23},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"God saw the Israelites and took notice.","from":23},{"book":"2KI","chapter":14,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"and since the LORD had said that He would not blot out the name of Israel from under heaven, He saved them by the hand of Jeroboam son of Jehoash.","from":23},{"book":"MIC","chapter":7,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Who is a God like You, who pardons iniquity and passes over the transgression of the remnant of His inheritance— who does not retain His anger forever, because He delights in loving devotion?","from":23},{"book":"MIC","chapter":7,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"You will show faithfulness to Jacob and loving devotion to Abraham, as You swore to our fathers from the days of old.","from":23},{"book":"EZK","chapter":37,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"The hand of the LORD was upon me, and He brought me out by His Spirit and set me down in the middle of the valley, and it was full of bones.","from":21},{"book":"EZK","chapter":37,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"So I prophesied as He had commanded me, and the breath entered them, and they came to life and stood on their feet—a vast army.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]}}